;;; A pattern's argument `(eq ?a ?b)` matches a stored `(eq Ann Bob)` by its shape —
;;; M1f **W82**, register row `W82/eq-value-matched-by-shape`, filed by S1f.7.10 (T1f.7.10.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, what each says, `(says Ann (eq Ann Bob))` and `(says Bob (eq Bob
;;; Bob))`, and a rule that believes them: `(says ?g (eq ?a ?b))` concludes `(same ?a
;;; ?b)`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; As a premise `(eq ?a ?b)` holds only of two equal values; as a pattern's argument
;;; it would be a second meaning of the one spelling. Refused at the parse, at the
;;; first `eq` a fact holds, on every command.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads, and the rule derives `(same Ann Bob)`, of two
;;; names that are not equal, and `(same Bob Bob)`, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.10 (T1f.7.10.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation says Guest Claim :why "{?1} says {?2}")
(relation same Guest Guest :why "{?1} and {?2} are the same guest")
(says Ann (eq Ann Bob))
(says Bob (eq Bob Bob))
(rule believe () :match (says ?g (eq ?a ?b)) :assert (same ?a ?b) :why "{?a} is {?b}: {?g} says so")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (same ?a ?b))
